## GRADING (binding; the ONE table for this gate; a shape is graded by it wherever it appears; capability decides, a comparison only finds candidates)
- **G-1/G-2 carried layer (C1, C3).** A byte of 0026, 0027, the 0026 recipe, a recipe SQL statement, `packages/db/src/**` or `apps/**` changed in the delta = **Blocker** (a pushed migration is final); the 0027 recipe changed beyond comment lines = **Blocker**; the end-to-end walk of C3 differing from the carried round-1 result (a dump after a recipe not equal to the previous schema, a recipe running when it must refuse, the previous build's `migrate` applying anything) = **Blocker/Major as round 1's G-2**; a pinned checksum unequal anywhere = **Blocker**.
- **G-3 the count query (C2).** The query printing a number different from the rows 0026 rejects = **Major**; **failing as printed in an interactive bash or zsh (history expansion, quoting) or in the Linux bash = Major** (the same class as B620-1: round 2 is its last chance); working in macOS shells and Linux bash not run = UNMEASURED, a Note, never a pass.
- **G-5 test validity (C1, C5, C6).** An existing assertion removed or loosened, a `.skip` / `.only` / `.todo` / `skipIf` / `retry` added = **Blocker**; a lost run-time name = **Major**; added other than the three = **Major**; a changed expected value that is not forced by its fixture = **Major**; **a new row no mutant turns red that is not a declared control = Major; the DEPLOY row not turning red under a planted `!` inside double quotes in either section = Major (it is B620-1's regression)**; a row that depends on the machine = **Minor** (**Major** if it can fail on a Linux runner); an id in a new title = **Minor**.
- **G-6 surviving mutant (C5, C6).** A survivor of u19, w26-14, x-G31-Staged (the round-2 targets) with the HEAD's files = **Major**; a round-1 kill lost = **Major** (unless proven equivalent by a forced run); a survivor on a behavioural rule of the CHECK, the index, a recipe guard (newest, checksum, ledger delete, drop, atomicity) = **Major** unless proven unreachable; a recipe-grant survivor at `b616-0026-down.db.test.ts:86` = **Minor** (the builder's own Note); a scanner-mutant survivor reachable by a DEPLOY.md text that a pty would print `event not found` for = **Major**, any other scanner survivor = **Minor** (weak) with its reachability stated, a shape outside the title's stated scope = **Note**; a mutant killed only by a pin or exact-definition row = **Minor** (weak).
- **G-7 operator words (C3, C4, C7).** A command in `DEPLOY.md` that fails as printed = **Major**; **a sentence the gate's measurement contradicts = Major** (including a new sentence that contradicts an unchanged one beside it); a changed or removed existing line OUTSIDE the two B616 sections = **Major**; a factual claim neither measured nor labelled unmeasured = **Minor**; a new sentence not on the builder's list = **Minor**; a printed runner line the real CLI of the named build does not print = **Major**; the Roll forward line unequal to this build's output = **Major**; a literal-but-misleading reading of a true sentence = **Note**; any user-facing, API or contract sentence in the delta = **Major** (none expected).
- **G-8 CI and CodeQL (C9, C10).** A failing check-run on the head or the merge result = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict: `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FINDINGS; a missing analysis is NOT scanned; an open alert on the PR ref = **Blocker**; a group red in your own image at the head = **Major** (a red you cannot reproduce twice is UNMEASURED).
- **G-9 overlap, hygiene, claims (C1, C10, C11).** A path shared with #85, #86, #88 or another live lane = **Major**; a conflict at merge against current main or in either order with #88 = Major for the merge order (Tuesday's call); a person's name, a real customer name or a secret in an added line, a commit message or a new file name = **Blocker**; a ticket key, `B620-n`/`B616`/`B593-n` id or BACKLOG row in a comment or commit message = **Note**, in a test title = **Minor**; a builder claim your measurement contradicts (1 commit, 6 paths, +153 -13, 38 / 461, 164, unit 3103+1, names lost 0 added 3, API db 79 / 1410, killed u19 / w26-14 / x-G31-Staged, `15` in both shells) = **Major**. **Always Note:** the builder's process disclosures (the stray-file exec, the extra image, the REFUSE-7 string), style, CI pending at the verdict (stated), the squash artefact, the Findings of FACT of round 1 (the unconstrained sibling `char(64)` columns, next free migration 0028, lookups the index does not narrow).
- **G-CAP.** A round-2 NO GO of the same class as a round-1 Major goes to the product owner, not to a round 3 (see TESTING).

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route, the round-1 gate's numbers)
8 cores shared with sibling Composer seats and the HPSM-POC, NexusAI and MPS seats; machine load1 reads 6-11 tonight (drafter 06:04: 7.31 6.32 6.50). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container run, `npm run ci:node`, any vitest over more than one file, a mutant run, the end-to-end walk, the Linux pty container. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do the light work meanwhile (C1 static, C7 sentence table, C8 static, C10 polling and the clone, the predictions). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind your own `mkdir` lock `<project>/.tools/b633/lock` (no other seat's lock; released by MOVE to `.tools/b633/quarantine/locks/`, never `rmdir`); the copied `heavy.sh` already runs the cross-seat `ps` gate (`ps -axo pid,command | /usr/bin/grep -E 'Datasec Security Composer|pc-b[0-9]+'` then `docker (build|compose|run)|vitest|scripts/ci.sh|dbtest.sh`, excluding your own tag): read it whole, quote the diff, and wait for another seat's heavy job and log the wait. A MOVING heartbeat (a counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b633/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` or `ps ... | grep` on a pattern that appears in its own command line: wait on a PID you recorded with `kill -0`, on `wait $!`, or on a done-marker file the job writes last. Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). Never leave a background job running when you finish. NO artificial load. A database test red ONLY under load and green re-run alone at load1 below 6 is a load artefact, not a finding: run it once alone and record both. **Database route:** the copied wrapper (throwaway `postgres:16` pinned by digest on `docker network create --internal`, no published port, a per-run generated password never written to disk, `PC_NODE_CI_IMAGE` required, the tree's `packages/` and `apps/` mounted read-only over the CI image; `B633_MOUNTS` is the `|`-separated list of extra host:container pairs, each mounted `:ro`; `B633_HOST_SCRIPT` runs a script of yours with `B633_DB`, `B633_NET`, `B633_IMAGE`, `B633_PW` in its environment only: use it for psql sessions, recipes, the real `migrate`, the pty runs and your seeding; no password on any argv or file you write). Build `pc-b633-node:{base,head}` with `docker build --pull=false -f docker/Dockerfile --target ci` from `-base` and `-head` (the builder's images are not yours); record node, npm, bash and PostgreSQL server versions. Remove ONLY your own `pc-b633-*` db container, anonymous volume and internal network, by exact name, after the log is saved.

